    "System.Description": "<div><b>As a</b> Report Author </div><div><b>I want</b> to set whether periodic data flows horizontally (across columns) or vertically (down rows) when I create a template </div><div><b>So that</b> the template's layout matches the report structure I need, before I begin linking variables </div><div><br> </div><div><b>Size estimate:</b> TBD � shell created for estimation </div><div><b>Sequencing note:</b> Logically precedes variable linking (1869322) � orientation should be set before an Author starts linking variables, since changing it later clears existing links. </div><div><br> </div><div><b>Requirements</b> </div><div><br> </div><div><b>Set orientation</b> </div><div>Author sets time-series orientation (horizontal/vertical) as a one-time setup decision, early in template creation. </div><div><br> </div><div><b>Destructive change warning</b> </div><div>Changing orientation after variables are already linked clears all existing links in the template. Author must be warned with a confirmation dialog and must confirm before this destructive action proceeds. </div><div><br> </div><div><b>Orientation applies template-wide</b> </div><div>Once set, all periodic variable links in the template follow the chosen orientation � this is a template-level structural setting, not a per-link property. </div>",
